WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.816
SPEAKER 1: Did you
know that you can now

00:00:01.816 --> 00:00:05.390
search every moment of every
video file in your catalog?

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.410
Google Cloud Video
Intelligence quickly

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.440
annotates videos stored
in Google Cloud Storage

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.410
and helps you identify key
nouns within your video

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.870
and when they occur
within the video.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.180
On this episode of
Google Cloud Labs,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.250
we'll introduce you to a
quick lab that shows you

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.540
how Cloud Video
Intelligence makes videos

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.950
searchable and discoverable
by extracting metadata

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.980
with an easy to use REST API.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.910
You'll create a request file and
call the Video Intelligence API

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.970
to create an operation
to process your request.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.360
You will run the operation.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:41.430
When it's complete,
you can see your videos

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.080
annotated, helping you identify
key entities within the video.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.820
Cloud Video
Intelligence allows you

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.910
to extract actionable
insights from video files

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.510
without requiring any machine
learning or computer vision

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.540
knowledge.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.630
From our massive library
of 20,000 labels,

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.360
it automatically
analyzes video content

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.360
to identify what entities
are in your video content

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.450
and when they appear.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.590
Cloud Video Intelligence
improves over time

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:12.420
as new concepts are introduced
and accuracy is improved.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.842
This lab is part of a series
of labs called QuickStarts.

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.300
These labs are
designed to give you

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.280
a little taste of
the many features

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.010
available within Google Cloud.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.770
Search for QuickStarts
in the lab catalog

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.267
to find the next lab
you'd like to take.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.600
When you're ready, use this
link to take the lab we just

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.010
went through today.

